lifeos-nix patch f-derived-watch-wire — wire DerivedWatch into Pulse loadModules

PROBLEM
  DerivedSync (regenerates PRINCIPAL_TELOS / LIFEOS_STATE / Data-Plane on USER edits) has no
  Linux on-change trigger — upstream ships only launchd WatchPaths (macOS). 7.40.4 confirms:
  no derived-watch module, no inotify wiring. Without it derived artifacts refresh only on
  the daily cron / install_core, so a mid-day TELOS edit leaves the @-imported PRINCIPAL_TELOS
  stale until the next run.

FIX
  Ship a DerivedWatch module (LIFEOS/PULSE/modules/derived-watch.ts, added in installPhase 1b)
  and wire it into pulse.ts loadModules: inotify (fs.watch) on the USER source subtrees +
  debounce + single-flight, inside the Pulse process (no extra daemon, no polling). Default-on
  (config.derived_watch?.enabled !== false — undefined in 7.40.4's PulseConfig, so the gate is
  default-on, which is the intent); the daily derived-sync cron stays as safety-net.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One hunk in pulse.ts loadModules (import + start), inserted between the Assistant and
  Performance module blocks. The module file is added separately in installPhase. Disjoint
  from f-telos-source and f4-*. Re-generated against 7.40.4 loadModules (2026-08-27 migration).

VERIFICATION
  Post-build: module present in payload; Pulse boots and logs "[derived-watch] watching N
  USER dirs". Hunk via `git diff`, never hand-counted.

